# Rust. `target*/`, not `target/`: a parallel build with `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target-x` writes a
# sibling the anchored rule would miss (tf_tree committed 358 MiB that way).
/target*/
**/*.rs.bk

# The bench gate's blessed samples (`docs/PHASE1.md` §9). `baseline/HOST.md` IS committed -- it
# names the host its floors were measured on -- but the samples are not: an accuracy maximum is a
# function of the source and the corpus alone (D16), so it travels; a timing is a property of one
# core under one load and does not. `cargo xtask bench-gate --bless` rewrites them in minutes.
/baseline/bench/

# Conformance run output (`docs/PHASE1.md` §1); the corpus, sweeps and baseline are committed.
/conformance/results/

# Runners are workspace-excluded, so cargo gives each its own `target/`.
/runners/*/target/

# Python reference generator (`uv`).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# mdbook output.
/docs/book/

# Local agent state.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editors, OS.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.env
.env.*
